      "title": "SSO Error Page for Payment Gateway Users",
      "description": "We are seeing a high volume of SSO error pages for users attempting to access the Payment Gateway v2 in the ME production region. Over 500 users are affected. This is definitely an incomplete rollback problem. We pushed a change yesterday and tried to roll it back, but it looks like the old version didn't fully restore, causing the authentication handshake to fail. Please fix the rollback state immediately."
    },
    {
      "i": 4734,
      "title": "Queue Manager API Empty Responses and 429 Errors",
      "description": "We are observing a pattern of failures with the Queue Manager in the US-East production environment. Approximately 51 users are impacted. The API is returning empty response bodies for valid requests, which causes our webhook retry logic to exhaust its attempts. Additionally, we are receiving HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) errors from the API gateway, suggesting we are being rate-limited unexpectedly, possibly due to the empty responses causing our client to retry aggressively. We need assistance debugging whether the empty responses are a bug in the service or if the rate limiting is misconfigured."
    },
    {
      "i": 4735,
      "title": "SSO Session Expiry and Missing MFA in Staging",
      "description": "In our staging environment (ANZ region), we are encountering inconsistent behavior with the SSO Integration Module. Users report that their sessions are expiring much faster than the configured TTL, forcing frequent re-logins. Furthermore, when these re-logins occur, the MFA prompt is often not appearing, allowing users to bypass second-factor authentication or getting stuck if the system expects it but doesn't provide it. This is affecting about 73 test users and hindering our QA process. Please investigate the session management and MFA trigger logic in the staging config."
    },
